From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sophgo: drive GPIOB0 high as Sipeed's board init does

Sipeed's cvi_board_init() sets XGPIOB[0] (pad PWM0_BUCK) to a GPIO
output at high level on every LicheeRV Nano based board. Some NanoKVM
Lite units need it for Ethernet: without it the PHY never gets a link
partner and eth0 stays at NO-CARRIER. Linux does not claim the pad, so
the state set here holds.

Latch first, then direction, then the pinmux, so the pad never drives
low as an output. Only bit 0 of the GPIOB registers changes.

---
--- a/board/sophgo/licheerv_nano/board.c
+++ b/board/sophgo/licheerv_nano/board.c
@@ -39,5 +39,14 @@
 	 */
 	writel(0x11, (void __iomem *)0x05027078);

+	/* XGPIOB[0] on pad PWM0_BUCK: output, high. Sipeed's board init does
+	 * this on every board; some NanoKVM Lite units have no Ethernet link
+	 * without it. Latch, direction, then the pinmux, so the pad never
+	 * drives low.
+	 */
+	setbits_le32((void __iomem *)0x03021000, BIT(0)); /* data: high */
+	setbits_le32((void __iomem *)0x03021004, BIT(0)); /* direction: out */
+	writel(3, (void __iomem *)0x030010ec);             /* pinmux: XGPIOB_0 */
+
 	return 0;
 }
--
